Third-party material

Software dependencies are listed in Cargo.lock. One is under a weak-copyleft licence: the acadrust
crate (DWG reading and writing, https://github.com/hakanaktt/acadrust) is licensed under the
Mozilla Public License 2.0 and is used unmodified as a separate library (crates/dwg). Its source
is available from crates.io and the repository above.

DWG is read and written first with BlackCAD's DWG and DXF crates (cad-dwg, cad-dxf and the
cad-model crate they share), licensed under the MIT License or the Apache License, Version 2.0,
at your option, from https://github.com/withshalom/CAD (crates/cad-*). The rest of that
repository is not open source; CADCraft uses only those three crates.

The blackcad-native branch (crates/blackcad) also uses BlackCAD's engine, cad-core, from the same
repository, and with it BlackCAD's open cad-native crate (the .cad format, MIT OR Apache-2.0).
cad-core is NOT open source: it is proprietary (LicenseRef-Proprietary; all rights reserved by
its owner, and no licence to use, copy, modify or distribute it is granted without the owner's
written permission; see LICENSE in that repository). The code in crates/blackcad is MIT OR
Apache-2.0 like the rest of CADCraft, but any build that includes it, and with it cad-core, is
subject to cad-core's terms and is not open source. This applies to the blackcad-native branch only; CADCraft's main line does not
depend on cad-core.


